XRef::isRefEncrypted() called getStream() on the object a compressed xref
entry names as its object stream without checking that it is a stream;
Object::getStream() aborts on anything else. Reached through
Dict::lookupEnsureEncryptedIfNeeded() (Catalog /URI) in encrypted files.

Not fixed upstream as of d828315.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for
isRefEncrypted, "object stream is not a stream").

